# Start octo and wait for the OCTO> prompt
# Run a SELECT that takes 60 seconds (HANGTIME waits 10 seconds for each of the 6 rows of the names table)
# and press Ctrl-C after 1 second
PASS : Ctrl-C cancels the SELECT
# Press the Up arrow to recall the canceled SELECT from the history, then press Enter to run it again
# and press Ctrl-C after 1 second
PASS : Up arrow recalls the canceled SELECT
PASS : Ctrl-C cancels the recalled SELECT
# Run an INSERT that takes 6 seconds (HANGTIME waits 1 second for each row it inserts) and press Ctrl-C after 1 second
PASS : Ctrl-C cancels the INSERT
# Run [select count(*) from names;]
PASS : The canceled INSERT added no rows (the names table still has 6 rows)
# Run a SELECT that takes 6 seconds and send octo a SIGUSR1 (as MUPIP INTRPT does) after 1 second
PASS : A SIGUSR1 does not cancel the SELECT, which returns all 6 rows
PASS : The SIGUSR1 created a YDB_JOBEXAM.ZSHOW_DMP file
# Exit octo
